From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:24:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/win32, nvk: composed present through a D3D11 flip swap
 chain (NVK_HELIOS_WSI_COMPOSE=1)

Under a DWM on NVK, NVK's Win32 swapchains take the WSI's GDI path
(patch 50): a GPU copy into system memory, a CPU wait and copy, and a
StretchBlt per frame. A D3D11 application's frames instead reach DWM
through the Helios D3D11 driver's composed present.

With NVK_HELIOS_WSI_COMPOSE=1 a window swapchain does the same:

- the WSI creates a D3D11 device on the Helios adapter (the first DXGI
  adapter whose description names Helios, MESA_WSI_COMPOSE_ADAPTER=<n>
  picks one by index) and a DXGI flip-model swap chain for the window,
  kept on the surface across swapchain re-creations (ResizeBuffers);
- every swapchain image is a D3D11 shared texture of that device; the
  WSI opens it through D3DKMT and reads what the Helios KMD records for
  the allocation (HeliosWddmOpenIdentity: resource id, size;
  HeliosWddmAllocLayout: modifier, stride, offset), and NVK imports that
  resource id as the image's dedicated memory (patch 0031's shared
  surface import, wsi_device::win32.compose_import), so the application
  renders into the texture;
- a present (after the common CPU wait for the rendering) copies the
  texture into the back buffer on the D3D11 device, presents with sync
  interval 1 for FIFO and 0 otherwise, and waits for the copy before the
  image can be acquired again.

Any failure (no Helios adapter, D3D11 device, swap chain, texture, open,
an identity that is not an RM resource, a refused import) is logged and
the swapchain falls back to Helios scanout or GDI as before. The D3D11
side lives in wsi_common_win32_compose.cpp (d3d11.h and the
DirectX-Headers' d3d12.h do not mix); D3D11, DXGI and D3DKMT entry
points are loaded at run time. Formats: B8G8R8A8 and R8G8B8A8 (UNORM,
SRGB). Off by default.
